# Decision Workflow

Purpose:
  Decision lifecycle from proposal to closure, including task mapping
  and chain integration.

States:
  proposed:
    Next: review|rejected
    Who: AI or Human

  review:
    Next: approved|rejected|revised
    Who: Human or Agent
    Gate: human approval required for architectural/security/business

  approved:
    Next: implemented
    Who: Human
    Gate: approval recorded
    Action: create tasks, link to decision

  rejected:
    Next: archived
    Who: Human
    Gate: feedback recorded

  revised:
    Next: review
    Who: AI
    Gate: revision feedback incorporated

  implemented:
    Next: verified
    Who: AI or Human
    Gate: tasks completed

  verified:
    Next: closed
    Who: Human or QA
    Gate: verification criteria met

  superseded:
    Next: archived
    Who: Human
    Gate: new decision approved
    Action: migrate tasks to new decision

  archived:
    Final state

Flow:
  proposed -> review -> approved -> implemented -> verified -> closed
                    -> rejected -> archived
                    -> revised -> review
                    -> superseded -> archived

ChainIntegration:
  D0 -> D1 (docs):
    Decision proposed during docs generation
  Human approval:
    Required before S1 (sdd) for architectural/security/business
  D0 -> S1 (sdd):
    Approved decision converted to tasks
  D0 -> C1 (code):
    Tasks implemented, decision -> implemented
  D0 -> R1 (review):
    Review completed, decision -> verified
  D0 -> DEP1 (deploy):
    Deployment verified, decision -> closed

TaskMapping:
  Every approved decision MUST create at least one task.
  Every task MUST reference its parent decision ID.
  Decision status MUST update as tasks progress.
  Superseded decisions MUST migrate tasks to new decision.

Rules:
  [DW1] Every significant change MUST have a decision record.
  [DW2] Architectural decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW3] Security decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW4] AI MAY propose technical decisions.
  [DW5] Human MAY override AI decisions.
  [DW6] Superseded decisions MUST reference new decision.
  [DW7] Conflicting decisions MUST be resolved before implementation.
  [DW8] Decision rationale MUST be recorded.
  [DW9] Implementation MUST reference decision ID.
  [DW10] Verification MUST reference decision criteria.
  [DTL1] Every approved decision MUST create at least one task.
  [DTL2] Every task MUST reference its parent decision.
  [DTL3] Decision status MUST update as tasks progress.
  [DTL4] Verification MUST run before decision is closed.
  [DTL5] Superseded decisions MUST migrate tasks to new decision.

State: +